    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so my monstera deliciosa has been looking kinda rough lately. i noticed a few of the lower leaves are turning yellow and they're feeling a bit soft/mushy. i've been watering it about once a week? not sure if i should change anything or if it needs more food or something. help!",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yellowing, soft, mushy lower leaves on your Monstera deliciosa are a classic sign of overwatering, which is probably the main issue here. It sounds like the roots are getting too much moisture and are starting to rot, which is a very common problem with indoor plants. Try to let the top couple of inches of soil dry out completely between waterings, and maybe even repot it into fresh, well-draining soil if it's been in the same pot for a long time. Good drainage is key, so make sure your pot has drainage holes!",
      "source": "target",
