    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the tip. i'll try letting it dry out more. i'm just worried because it happened so fast... like, it looked fine one day and then suddenly a few leaves were yellow/mushy. do you think it could be something else though? maybe like a pest or something hidden in the soil?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While overwatering is the most likely culprit, sudden decline can sometimes signal a hidden pest infestation, so keep an eye out for tiny, unwelcome guests. You can check the undersides of the leaves and the soil surface for any signs of tiny bugs, like spider mites or fungus gnats. If you see any webbing or tiny black specks, treat it immediately, but remember that even a small amount of root rot can make a plant look like it's being attacked by a plague of pests. A little bit of root rot can spread faster than a scouting party of tiny gnats!",
